      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1273462387,
      "text": "Triumfetta rhomboidea, commonly known as diamond burbark, Chinese bur, or kulutkulutan in Tagalog, is a shrub that is extensively naturalised in tropical regions.\nIt is thought that to have come to Australia from China. Its bark—sometimes called burbark—makes a kind of jute."
    }
